docs/findings/README.md:26: | [649_RESOURCE_MAP_AND_SENSITIVITY.md](649_RESOURCE_MAP_AND_SENSITIVITY.md) | Side project of the #229 area epic and input to #640 (#649): the shipping 1x1 route at dev `241f9184` mapped to every one of its 175 blocks, each block's LUT, FF, RAMB and DSP figures read from both the utilization report and the placed-cell census, its CARRY4 and slices from the census, and the totals tied to the `route-1x1` record, and the resource cost of every design parameter: 59 Yosys sweep points (52 guard-clean, 7 refused), four Vivado anchors at 1, 2, 4 and 8 streams, the SoC options with the CPU, cache and L2 variants priced out of context from a scratch recipe copy, and the redundancy second port | Current, measurement only. Each stream per direction costs 3,828 LUT out of context, two thirds in the processor, with a falling cost per added stream; channels and the TDM capture width cost nothing; the low-function-cost prunes total up to about 1,200 routed LUT, a tenth of the NFR-RES-01 gap. At the measurement revision, Yosys ignored converted elaboration guards. Since #651, both synthesis flows refuse active guards. At the measurement revision the builder accepted an 8x8 TDM8 configuration the saved-state backend refused (235 names against 128); since #652 the builder refuses that shape before generation. |
